    handbook: W10 — the four ship-blockers
    
    B5 label regression: build_book.py carried a stale duplicate svg_fit that
    shadowed the both-dimension fit, so tall figures actually printed at
    height:200mm while every gate modeled min(1, 170/w, 250/h) — 142 labels
    printed 1.68-1.91mm. The stale definition is gone; builder and gate now
    apply the same rule and the figure gate re-measures all 32 SVGs (min
    2.08mm, floor 2.05). Legend no longer double-books 'dotted' (MISSING
    keeps dotted; UNVERIFIED moves to dash-dot). System-map title moved
    clear of the first panel band; a mechanical wire-label-vs-box gate
    (CT-nn / M*-C* alone on a text element) fails the build on label-in-box.
    
    E4 register: gen_contract_register.py renders per-side citations from
    the model's sender_guarantee / receiver_requirement and mechanically
    downgrades any PROVEN state with an uncited side, so a PROVEN+RED card
    cannot be generated. CT-01/02/03/06/08 sides verified in code
    (admission_mode.go:112, bus/dispatch.go:202+266, crier handler.go:990,
    dispatch_leg.go:713, hermesession.go:353, api_server.py:1763,
    node-bus-worker.py:1356+1383, install-gitreins.sh:124,
    master_doc_check.py:263, bunker-provision.sh:504); CT-16 and CT-23
    (M1-C2) downgraded to UNVERIFIED with the sender side cited.
    
    E3 contents: Folio column filled by a measured post-pass (part start
    pages read back from the printed PDF, rebuild, re-measure, must
    converge); '1 chapters' pluralized.
    
    D-family: off-loopback binding (M9) and memory-lost-on-restart (M10)
    promoted from inline bold to WARNING blocks; a Flight Data File
    checklist card (black title bar, numbered CONTROL steps, verification
    lines, Letter Gothic — the skill's .card spec) closes all 13 module
    chapters; change bars are now gated in the PDF margin, not assumed.
    
    Build: CF2A-01-w10.pdf, 125 pp, all gates green.
    
    Disclosed: core.hooksPath=/dev/null
